{"book":19,"chapter":41,"context":{"chapter":41,"title":"Betrayed by a Close Friend","summary":"David blesses those who care for the weak, then describes lying sick while enemies hope for his death and even a trusted friend turns on him. Book I closes with a doxology.","background":"Title: 'To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.' Some connect the betrayal with Ahithophel, David's counselor who joined Absalom (2 Samuel 15:31), though the psalm does not name him. Jesus quotes verse 9 about Judas (John 13:18). Verse 13 is the doxology that ends Book I.","customs":[{"term":"Eating my bread","verses":"41:9","note":"Sharing a meal created a bond of loyalty; betraying a table companion was especially shameful."}],"watchFor":["The ending 'Amen, and Amen' (v. 13) closes the first of the Psalter's five books."],"connections":["John 13:18","2 Samuel 15:31","Psalms 55:12-14","Psalms 72:18-19"]},"verses":{"0":{"w":[["לַמְנַצֵּחַ","lamnatzeach","H5329","HRd/Vprmsa","to the choirmaster"],["מִזְמוֹר","mizmor","H4210","HNcmsa","a psalm"],["לְדָוִד","ledavid","H1732","HR/Npm","of David"]]},"1":{"w":[["אַשְׁרֵי","'ashrei","H835","HNcmpc","how blessed!"],["מַשְׂכִּיל","maskil","H7919","HVhrmsa","[is one who] considers"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","<to>"],["דָּל","dal","H1800","HAamsa","[the] poor"],["בְּיוֹם","beyom","H3117","HR/Ncmsc","in a day of"],["רָעָה","ra'ah","H7451","HNcfsa","trouble"],["יְמַלְּטֵהוּ","yemaletehu","H4422","HVpi3ms/Sp3ms","he will deliver him"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"]],"x":[[20019017,20019017,31],[20014021,20014021,21],[47009008,47009014,20],[44020035,44020035,19],[40025034,40025039,16],[19037039,19037040,15],[59002013,59002013,11],[19037019,19037019,10],[58006010,58006010,10],[19112009,19112009,9]],"xn":25},"2":{"w":[["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["יִשְׁמְרֵהוּ","yishmerehu","H8104","HVqi3ms/Sp3ms","he will keep him"],["וִיחַיֵּהוּ","vichaiyehu","H2421","HC/Vpu3ms/Sp3ms","and he will preserve alive him"],["וְאֻשַּׁר","ve'usha